# Copy this file to .env.local and keep only the lines you need.

# Local JSON archive. Without it the app uses data/recipes.json in this folder.
# A relative path starts from this folder.
# DATA_FILE=data/recipes.json

# Neon Postgres. When set, it replaces the local file.
# In Neon Console, open your project and choose Connect to copy the connection string.
# Never commit the real value or place it in browser code.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# Shared password of the single-kitchen app. Without a database it guards the app (optional on your
# own computer). With a database everyone has an account, and this password is only asked once:
# the first account must type it to take the data that existed before accounts.
# APP_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-password

# Accounts (Better Auth, only with DATABASE_URL). A long random secret that signs the sessions;
# without it one is derived from DATABASE_URL. Changing it signs everyone out.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
# Public address of the app, when it differs from the Vercel production URL.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://your-app.example.com

# Reading invoice photos in Food Stock → Deliveries.
# Free key: https://aistudio.google.com → Get API key. Never commit the real value.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key
# Optional: one Gemini model to use. Without it the app picks the newest Flash models the key can use.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
# Which service reads invoices (default gemini). "demo" returns a sample invoice for local tests.
# INVOICE_READER=gemini
